# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE LIVE PAGES LOAD FROM vendor/            (rewritten 2026-08-12, v7)
#
# The v7 rebuild retired the cortical-mesh hero, and with it every heavy asset
# this file used to guard. The 2026-08-12 prune deleted 44 files -- the meshes
# and their .npy sources, the tract-line bundle, the bloom/bokeh pipeline, the
# HDR environment, MarchingCubes, GSAP, ScrollTrigger, Lenis, the three.js
# module build, and the old font set -- taking vendor/ from 12.7 MB to 0.8 MB.
#
# Everything left in vendor/ IS loaded by a live page. There is nothing here to
# exclude any more, which is why this section has no rules under it:
#
#   vendor/fonts/*.woff2     16 faces, latin subset, one file per weight used
#                            index.html  -> archivo 500-900, ibm-plex-mono 400-600
#                            neural.html -> syne 600-800, dm-sans 400/500/700,
#                                           dm-mono 400/500
#   vendor/three.min.js      three r128 UMD build, used by neural.html only
#   vendor/three-LICENSE.txt MIT licence text that ships with it
#
# Both pages now make ZERO third-party requests for assets. Fonts and three.js
# are self-hosted; the only outbound requests are the links a visitor clicks and
# the Super Bowl Squares iframe, which loads only after an explicit click.
#
# The rule learned the hard way, still in force:
#
#   DO NOT use `vendor/*` + `!vendor/fonts/`. That pattern is correct under
#   git's matcher (verified) but Vercel did NOT honour the directory
#   re-include: deployed 2026-08-05, /vendor/fonts/IBMPlexSans-400.woff2 came
#   back 404 and the live site silently fell back to system fonts. If anything
#   in vendor/ ever needs excluding again, exclude it EXPLICITLY by name, with
#   no negation to get wrong.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the pages. After ANY deploy, verify against the
# deployed URL, not against git: an ignore pattern that git accepts proves
# nothing about how the host treats it.
#
# NOTE: the archived pages under design-candidates/archive/ still reference the
# deleted mesh and font assets. They are kept as a record of what shipped, not
# as runnable pages, and they are not deployed. Recover assets from git history
# if one ever needs to run again.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
